A(('p', '13.2 Neighboring parables. The Ten Virgins, the Talents, the Faithful and Unfaithful Servant and the Wheat and the Weeds are each read in their own study of the Parable Studies. This account makes no use of their meanings, and they make none of this.'))
A(('p', '13.3 Final Synthesis. The Son of man comes in his glory and sits on the throne of his glory. All nations are gathered before him, and he separates them as a shepherd divides his sheep from the goats, setting the sheep on his right hand and the goats on the left. He tells the right hand to inherit the kingdom prepared for them, and the left hand to depart into everlasting fire, each according to what was done or not done for the hungry, the thirsty, the stranger, the naked, the sick and the prisoner. The King says that what was done or not done to one of the least of these was done or not done to him, and the account closes on everlasting punishment and life eternal. He names nothing else.'))
